WEBVTT

00:04.170 --> 00:07.007
<i>The True Demon King has died.</i>

00:07.007 --> 00:10.927
<i>The enemy of the world
was defeated by somebody.</i>

00:10.927 --> 00:16.141
<i>But even now, the powers left behind
writhe in multitude.</i>

00:16.141 --> 00:19.477
<i>They cannot be subdued
by ordinary strength.</i>

00:19.477 --> 00:22.230
<i>A hundred</i> shura<i>-like demons...</i>

00:23.773 --> 00:28.695
<i>The world's largest city, Aureatia,
proceeds with the selection of a Hero,</i>

00:29.446 --> 00:32.949
<i>while the leader
of the New Principality of Lithia,</i>

00:32.949 --> 00:38.079
<i>Taren the Guarded,
seeks new order, and governs through fear.</i>

00:51.676 --> 00:55.055
ISHURA

02:09.045 --> 02:12.924
Episode 11
When the Sun Sets

02:12.924 --> 02:17.470
New Principality of Lithia

02:45.165 --> 02:48.168
Get out, Yuno the Distant Talon.

02:49.460 --> 02:50.461
Dakai...

02:51.045 --> 02:54.090
What is it? I've come to help you
just like I said I would.

02:54.090 --> 02:57.093
H-How can you say that right now?

02:57.093 --> 02:59.846
Isn't your army at war right now?

03:00.513 --> 03:03.266
Do you have time
to come help the likes of me?

03:03.266 --> 03:04.601
It's not my army.

03:05.185 --> 03:06.811
Lithia is finished.

03:06.811 --> 03:09.022
There's nothing else that can be done.

03:09.022 --> 03:12.192
Even so, I want to keep
the promise I made.

03:13.943 --> 03:17.363
It's not your fault
that Higuare got you involved.

03:17.363 --> 03:19.449
Then there's the whole thing with Nagan.

03:20.283 --> 03:22.785
I may be a villain,

03:22.785 --> 03:24.913
but I've never lied.

03:24.913 --> 03:26.956
Cut the crap!

03:26.956 --> 03:31.211
Just because you're strong, you don't care
that your city has been destroyed?

03:31.211 --> 03:33.546
Doesn't it hurt you or make you sad?

03:33.546 --> 03:35.757
Won't you fight until your last breath?

03:36.466 --> 03:37.508
<i>As for me...</i>

03:40.929 --> 03:43.765
<i>I feel like I'm in the depths of hell,</i>

03:43.765 --> 03:46.601
<i>just because one person died.</i>

03:47.644 --> 03:49.062
Good question.

03:49.062 --> 03:51.564
I don't particularly care anymore.

03:51.564 --> 03:54.317
It is true that I liked Miss Taren,

03:55.068 --> 03:57.737
but so long as I'm alive,
I'm sure I'll meet somebody else.

03:57.737 --> 04:00.406
Wait! Dakai the Magpie!

04:00.406 --> 04:03.076
Is there something else I can do for you?

04:03.076 --> 04:06.162
You told me to take revenge now
if I want to, right?

04:06.913 --> 04:09.582
From Yuno to the Arrowhead of Fipike.
Index finger axis. Lattice star.

04:09.582 --> 04:10.875
Exploding sparks.

04:10.875 --> 04:12.210
Spin!

04:23.096 --> 04:24.764
Are you serious about fighting me?

04:32.105 --> 04:34.524
Curte, you must flee right now.

04:35.108 --> 04:36.526
Slowpoke.

04:36.526 --> 04:39.696
Regnejee, w-why...

04:41.447 --> 04:44.117
Regnejee, is this your blood?

04:44.117 --> 04:47.287
I can't believe you would ever lose.

04:47.870 --> 04:49.706
It's over for Lithia.

04:49.706 --> 04:51.874
I'm indebted to Taren,

04:51.874 --> 04:53.126
and my swarm.

04:55.628 --> 04:58.715
I protected them this whole time.

04:59.299 --> 05:03.303
I built up the swarm.
I ruled over them, and guided them.

05:03.303 --> 05:06.055
That worthless bunch of scum.

05:06.055 --> 05:07.807
They got what they deserved.

05:08.391 --> 05:11.811
<i>But everything's ruined now.</i>

05:12.729 --> 05:15.231
<i>At the very end though...</i>

05:15.231 --> 05:18.067
<i>I won at the very end, Curte.</i>

05:18.735 --> 05:20.320
My treasure...

05:29.329 --> 05:31.080
Run, Curte.

05:31.080 --> 05:33.916
Before the Aureatian army gets here.

05:33.916 --> 05:37.587
At least you should make it out.

05:37.587 --> 05:40.340
I'll win in the end,

05:40.340 --> 05:42.759
Alus the Star Runner.

05:42.759 --> 05:44.594
You'll see.

05:45.178 --> 05:46.179
Regnejee...

05:50.767 --> 05:51.768
Don't move!

05:51.768 --> 05:52.852
Oh!

05:53.978 --> 05:55.313
No way.

05:55.897 --> 05:56.981
Surely not.

05:57.940 --> 05:59.108
Who are you?

05:59.108 --> 06:03.112
I am the Sixth General
of the Twenty-Nine Officials of Aureatia,

06:03.112 --> 06:04.947
Harghent the Still.

06:05.782 --> 06:07.784
I came here to defeat a foreign enemy,

06:07.784 --> 06:10.119
upon the request of Mage City citizens.

06:10.119 --> 06:12.789
Aureatia... I see.

06:12.789 --> 06:15.625
So everything really is over.

06:18.711 --> 06:20.713
Are you a prisoner of war?

06:20.713 --> 06:22.382
Or a citizen?

06:29.972 --> 06:30.973
Stop!

06:30.973 --> 06:33.226
You mustn't protect it.

06:33.226 --> 06:36.729
It is a dreadful creature
that has massacred people.

06:36.729 --> 06:40.316
As a member of the minian races,
I must ensure that it is vanquished.

06:40.316 --> 06:42.026
Regnejee...

06:42.610 --> 06:44.904
...is a friend of mine.

06:45.530 --> 06:48.699
He helped me more than any minia did.

06:48.699 --> 06:49.784
He's a dear friend.

06:49.784 --> 06:51.452
You are still

06:51.452 --> 06:53.788
a young girl.

06:53.788 --> 06:56.582
You mustn't burden yourself
with such a crime.

06:59.168 --> 07:00.586
Please.

07:00.586 --> 07:02.922
Many people have died.

07:02.922 --> 07:04.590
Too many.

07:04.590 --> 07:05.800
The truth is,

07:05.800 --> 07:09.637
I have no desire to kill people either.

07:09.637 --> 07:10.888
So please.

07:10.888 --> 07:12.640
I knew.

07:12.640 --> 07:14.809
I just pretended that I didn't.

07:15.393 --> 07:16.644
I knew this whole time.

07:17.186 --> 07:19.772
What I was doing.

07:19.772 --> 07:22.191
And what Regnejee was.

07:25.153 --> 07:26.195
Stop!

07:26.195 --> 07:29.699
You've always been my angel,

07:30.283 --> 07:31.451
Regnejee.

07:33.536 --> 07:34.579
Don't! Stop.

07:35.163 --> 07:37.165
That is an enemy of the minian races.

07:37.165 --> 07:39.333
Keep your mouth shut, trash.

07:39.333 --> 07:42.837
You incompetent, foolish piece of trash.

07:42.837 --> 07:44.755
Don't say one more word to Curte.

07:44.755 --> 07:45.923
That thing

07:46.424 --> 07:47.967
is a wyvern!

07:59.187 --> 08:00.188
Huh?

08:07.987 --> 08:09.071
Curte...

08:24.670 --> 08:26.672
Regnejee...

08:43.523 --> 08:45.441
Don't make fun

08:46.025 --> 08:47.693
of my friend.

08:53.115 --> 08:55.451
Alus... Alus!

08:55.451 --> 08:56.911
Alus!

08:56.911 --> 08:59.413
Curse you!

08:59.997 --> 09:01.582
One always helps a friend.

09:02.458 --> 09:03.876
Isn't that obvious?

09:06.045 --> 09:07.463
I'll get help.

09:14.720 --> 09:16.722
Regnejee...

09:42.206 --> 09:43.791
You really were

09:44.667 --> 09:47.003
a wyvern.

10:21.245 --> 10:22.330
Who is it?

10:23.497 --> 10:25.833
Would you believe me
if I said I was an angel?

10:26.626 --> 10:28.461
I've come for you, young lady.

10:28.461 --> 10:31.631
Is that so? Thank you.

10:32.214 --> 10:34.216
On that day too,

10:34.216 --> 10:37.053
somebody sang the song of an angel.

10:40.264 --> 10:43.434
The truth is, there's something

10:43.434 --> 10:46.187
that I've always wished for.

10:46.187 --> 10:50.524
Everybody has a right to be saved.

10:50.524 --> 10:52.443
Wish for whatever you like.

10:54.278 --> 10:55.613
Mom...

10:57.323 --> 10:59.241
My mom...

11:11.545 --> 11:13.047
How many have I killed?

11:23.724 --> 11:26.811
This is quite a fitting end
for a self-proclaimed Demon King,

11:26.811 --> 11:27.895
Taren.

11:28.979 --> 11:32.775
Shalk. You've been working hard too.

11:32.775 --> 11:36.445
I've not really been working.

11:36.445 --> 11:37.655
Well,

11:37.655 --> 11:40.324
it doesn't seem that way.

11:40.324 --> 11:42.660
Do you regret starting a losing battle?

11:42.660 --> 11:43.828
Not at all.

11:44.578 --> 11:48.999
If one chooses to engage in battle,
they should be prepared to accept defeat.

11:49.750 --> 11:52.002
Actually, no...

11:53.879 --> 11:55.047
That's a lie.

11:55.715 --> 11:58.050
The truth is
I regret that I couldn't

11:58.050 --> 11:59.218
bring them happiness.

11:59.218 --> 12:02.471
The soldiers who admired me,
the people, and Curte.

12:03.597 --> 12:06.767
I regret that I will die
without being able to atone

12:06.767 --> 12:10.521
for dragging everyone into my pursuit

12:10.521 --> 12:11.772
of unknown ideals.

12:12.356 --> 12:13.357
I see.

12:14.525 --> 12:18.112
As a monarch,
I didn't have what it took to bring peace.

12:18.112 --> 12:21.574
Because all I've ever known
is the battlefield.

12:22.158 --> 12:23.325
Don't sweat it.

12:23.325 --> 12:24.952
I'm pretty much the same.

12:25.578 --> 12:28.080
Heck, I'm still this way
even now I'm dead.

12:29.749 --> 12:31.584
Shalk the Sound Slicer.

12:31.584 --> 12:33.836
You wished for information
on the Final Land

12:33.836 --> 12:37.047
where the True Demon King
met their end, didn't you?

12:37.047 --> 12:38.132
Right.

12:38.132 --> 12:39.967
Don't you find it strange?

12:39.967 --> 12:42.636
That nobody knows
who the True Demon King is.

12:42.636 --> 12:44.889
Not me, nor you.

12:44.889 --> 12:47.391
It is never spoken of.

12:47.892 --> 12:51.312
Yet everybody knows just how terrifying

12:51.312 --> 12:53.105
the True Demon King was.

12:53.105 --> 12:54.607
But I'm sure that

12:54.607 --> 12:58.569
the time will come when we must find out.

12:59.153 --> 13:00.738
I can't read.

13:00.863 --> 13:03.115
Then have someone read it for you.

13:03.115 --> 13:06.035
I've had reconnaissance squads
explore the Final Land several times,

13:06.035 --> 13:08.829
but each time they were thwarted.

13:09.413 --> 13:13.167
<i>Which means some unknown monster
must reside in the land.</i>

13:13.167 --> 13:14.835
<i>In that unexplored land...</i>

13:14.835 --> 13:18.172
<i>Still, we have managed to map some areas.</i>

13:18.923 --> 13:21.759
But the bodies of the Hero
and the True Demon King

13:21.759 --> 13:23.594
still haven't been found.

13:24.178 --> 13:26.597
That's all I need to know.

13:27.181 --> 13:30.392
I bet I could have helped you more,
had I worked harder.

13:31.101 --> 13:34.355
I can't offer you
any more reward than this.

13:37.817 --> 13:39.443
You're free to go where you like.

13:39.985 --> 13:42.905
I doubt it will do you any good
if people find out

13:42.905 --> 13:45.074
you served under a general like me.

13:45.074 --> 13:46.242
Right.

13:46.742 --> 13:50.579
I'm guessing someone will show up
to finish you off any moment now.

13:57.586 --> 13:59.588
Didn't have it in you
as a monarch, huh?

13:59.588 --> 14:03.092
I thought you'd make
a pretty good monarch.

14:03.092 --> 14:05.511
I'm no monarch.

14:06.512 --> 14:07.680
I'm a Demon King.

14:14.478 --> 14:18.315
You know, you'd better flee soon.

14:18.315 --> 14:20.651
Shut... up!

14:22.611 --> 14:25.865
I-I'll get you. Even just one punch!

14:25.865 --> 14:27.324
Is that right?

14:32.454 --> 14:34.790
You've had your one punch.
Are you done now?

14:35.374 --> 14:38.961
It's quite rare for me
to humor someone for this long.

14:44.133 --> 14:47.136
I doubt we'll meet again, Yuno.

14:49.054 --> 14:50.055
Wait!

15:00.399 --> 15:01.483
Yo.

15:01.984 --> 15:05.905
Ishura
Self-Proclaimed Demon King

15:10.993 --> 15:14.413
Looks like I finally found
someone interesting.

15:15.497 --> 15:16.665
From the very start,

15:17.499 --> 15:21.086
I never thought I could actually beat you.

15:21.086 --> 15:22.922
Not me.

15:22.922 --> 15:24.006
I see.

15:24.006 --> 15:28.344
I did find it strange how those arrows
up your sleeves were decreasing.

15:28.344 --> 15:32.932
I thought he might still be alive.

15:34.183 --> 15:36.435
<i>That he might make it in time.</i>

15:36.435 --> 15:38.854
<i>That you might not kill me.</i>

15:40.064 --> 15:42.441
<i>That you'd brush me off
even if I challenged you to a fight.</i>

15:43.901 --> 15:46.403
<i>Soujirou traveled with me.</i>

15:46.403 --> 15:48.447
<i>He would be able to distinguish my arrows.</i>

15:49.073 --> 15:51.492
<i>I knew it was a long shot.</i>

15:52.910 --> 15:55.829
These arrows are all I can fire.

15:56.413 --> 15:58.082
My second name

15:58.666 --> 16:00.668
is Yuno the Distant Talon.

16:04.046 --> 16:06.382
Hilarious. Amazing.

16:06.382 --> 16:07.633
I can't believe it!

16:07.633 --> 16:10.135
This girl got the better of me.

16:10.135 --> 16:13.055
Life is full of surprises.

16:13.055 --> 16:14.431
Oy.

16:15.015 --> 16:16.684
Is this the time to be laughing?

16:16.684 --> 16:17.893
Oh, yeah.

16:17.893 --> 16:21.981
Visitor. I've heard all about you.

16:21.981 --> 16:23.899
You're the swordsman who cut the spider.

16:30.489 --> 16:32.741
Seems you have yourself
a good sword.

16:32.741 --> 16:35.536
You don't look like a swordsman yourself.

16:35.536 --> 16:37.788
I like you.

16:37.788 --> 16:41.250
You're the first person who's got that.

16:41.834 --> 16:44.503
Didn't you go to assassinate Miss Taren?

16:44.503 --> 16:46.755
Wasn't that your job?

16:47.339 --> 16:48.757
Don't ask me.

16:48.757 --> 16:51.010
I just came here to fight.

16:51.593 --> 16:54.013
Something I haven't fought yet.

16:54.013 --> 16:56.348
Something worth fighting.

16:56.348 --> 16:58.767
Something that only exists in this world.

16:59.351 --> 17:01.603
Rather than going after
this so-called Taren,

17:01.603 --> 17:05.441
I thought following Yuno's arrows
might end up more interesting.

17:05.441 --> 17:06.775
That's why I've come.

17:06.775 --> 17:08.027
Soujirou...

17:08.777 --> 17:11.030
<i>I detest you...</i>

17:11.030 --> 17:12.281
<i>But still...</i>

17:12.281 --> 17:14.366
Let's stop the talking

17:14.366 --> 17:15.784
and fight already.

17:15.784 --> 17:17.369
There's no rush.

17:17.369 --> 17:19.329
One of us will die anyway.

17:19.955 --> 17:23.042
Why don't we reminisce
about the Distant World, Soujirou?

17:23.042 --> 17:25.544
I have no good memories of that place.

17:26.503 --> 17:30.049
<i>The food sucked.
People tried to kill me every day.</i>

17:30.049 --> 17:32.634
<i>I fought nobody but weaklings.</i>

17:33.886 --> 17:37.056
Before I knew it,
I'd arrived in this world.

17:37.056 --> 17:39.725
Yeah, it was the same for me.

17:39.725 --> 17:42.561
All these people have died,
yet it doesn't bother me.

17:45.564 --> 17:49.318
<i>Never once have I felt that
I missed the Distant World,</i>

17:49.318 --> 17:51.904
<i>or that I wanted to go back.</i>

17:51.904 --> 17:55.824
<i>Maybe visitors are all deviants like us.</i>

17:55.824 --> 17:58.077
<i>We're always alone
because we're too strong.</i>

17:58.911 --> 18:02.081
You're making it sound like
being too strong is a bad thing.

18:03.248 --> 18:06.335
Plenty of people do think so.

18:06.335 --> 18:08.837
But being alone is freedom.

18:08.837 --> 18:10.089
That's why

18:10.089 --> 18:13.175
I like who I am now.

18:13.175 --> 18:16.512
If there's any reason I was
cast out to this world,

18:16.512 --> 18:18.764
then that must be it.

18:19.807 --> 18:21.225
Kill him.

18:21.809 --> 18:23.185
<i>I know it myself.</i>

18:23.811 --> 18:25.979
<i>Who I really should have blamed that day.</i>

18:26.563 --> 18:28.565
<i>It was myself.</i>

18:28.565 --> 18:30.484
<i>Because I was weak.</i>

18:31.819 --> 18:32.986
<i>But...</i>

18:32.986 --> 18:35.239
<i>even if my hatred is misplaced,</i>

18:35.989 --> 18:38.158
<i>it's to save myself.</i>

18:39.368 --> 18:41.328
Kill him, Soujirou!

18:41.328 --> 18:43.580
If we're all free to do what we like,

18:43.580 --> 18:45.874
then I'm free
to wish for revenge, aren't I?

18:45.874 --> 18:47.459
Even if it's meaningless.

18:47.459 --> 18:49.545
Even if I know
it's a wicked thing to wish for.

18:49.545 --> 18:53.006
There's nobody who can criticize me,
is there?

18:53.006 --> 18:54.258
Right.

18:54.258 --> 18:58.011
Which means I'm also free
to decide whether to kill this guy or not.

18:58.011 --> 18:59.096
Jeez.

18:59.096 --> 19:02.599
I was just thinking
about getting the heck out of here.

19:02.599 --> 19:04.768
Well, don't worry.

19:04.768 --> 19:07.771
There's more than enough time left for me
to play with you.

19:14.361 --> 19:17.322
<i>This world had always
wished for it too.</i>

19:17.906 --> 19:20.784
<i>For someone else to come</i>

19:20.784 --> 19:22.786
<i>and defeat the True Demon King,</i>

19:22.786 --> 19:25.205
<i>that couldn't be beaten by anyone.</i>

19:34.590 --> 19:36.049
Here I come!

19:41.305 --> 19:42.723
<i>Not yet...</i>

19:42.723 --> 19:44.224
<i>Now!</i>

19:45.726 --> 19:48.645
<i>The absolute fastest enchanted sword</i>

19:48.645 --> 19:50.856
<i>takes the initiative in every fight.</i>

19:50.856 --> 19:57.946
<i>However, if the wielder's arm is held back
at the exact moment of its action...</i>

20:01.617 --> 20:03.785
<i>Simultaneous movement.</i>

20:03.785 --> 20:06.872
<i>A masterful technique,
faster than even the electric current</i>

20:07.456 --> 20:09.208
<i>that runs through consciousness.</i>

20:09.208 --> 20:10.375
Got it.

20:10.375 --> 20:11.627
Yeah.

20:11.627 --> 20:13.629
You're as good as they say.

20:13.629 --> 20:16.506
This is where your life is.

20:16.506 --> 20:19.009
You're right, but...

20:19.009 --> 20:22.596
<i>The true value
of this out-of-this-world bandit</i>

20:22.596 --> 20:24.932
<i>lies in his keen eyesight.</i>

20:26.391 --> 20:29.353
<i>Even when facing an exceptional swordsman,</i>

20:29.353 --> 20:32.856
<i>he can predict the future.</i>

20:33.941 --> 20:36.026
<i>He discerns everything.</i>

20:36.026 --> 20:38.779
<i>Including the scene before him
and the enemy's thoughts.</i>

20:38.779 --> 20:41.240
I have a monopoly on winning.

20:41.240 --> 20:45.118
<i>The bandit's sword
finally surpassed Yagyuu swordsmanship.</i>

20:48.413 --> 20:50.791
<i>T-This guy...</i>

20:51.833 --> 20:52.918
Heh.

20:52.918 --> 20:55.170
<i>His sword...</i>

20:55.754 --> 20:56.922
<i>It doesn't make sense.</i>

20:56.922 --> 21:00.175
<i>How did this sword
cut through the tarantula's armor?</i>

21:00.175 --> 21:02.803
I told you I had it.

21:02.803 --> 21:04.554
Your life!

21:04.554 --> 21:07.057
I-It was never

21:07.057 --> 21:09.309
an enchanted sword.

21:09.309 --> 21:12.062
Seems you have yourself
a good sword.

21:13.146 --> 21:16.566
<i>Did he predict all of this?</i>

21:16.566 --> 21:20.070
<i>How can another visitor be so much better?</i>

21:21.154 --> 21:23.824
<i>What should I do? What could I have done...</i>

21:23.824 --> 21:26.076
<i>to beat him?</i>

21:27.536 --> 21:30.038
<i>I can't believe it.</i>

21:30.038 --> 21:32.165
Well, you weren't wrong.

21:35.502 --> 21:37.796
You really aren't a swordsman.

23:36.540 --> 23:38.542
Translated by Zacarias Hicks

23:39.376 --> 23:40.961
Episode 12
Shura
